    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"105\">\r\n<p><strong>Syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"84\">\r\n<p><strong>Gene(s)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"161\">\r\n<p><strong>Mode of inheritance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"252\">\r\n<p><strong>Characteristic distinguishing clinical features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p>Polymerase proofreading&ndash;associated polyposis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>POLE</em> and <em>POLD1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal dominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>Multiple colorectal adenomas; personal and/or family history of endometrial, brain, or other LS-associated tumours; hypermutant phenotype on DNA sequencing {25110875}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p><em>MUTYH</em>-associated polyposis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>MUTYH</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal recessive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>Multiple colorectal adenomas; frequent G&rarr;T mutations on DNA sequencing {24953332}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p><em>NTHL1</em>-associated polyposis</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>NTHL1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal recessive</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>{25938944}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p>n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>FAN1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal dominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>{26052075; 28577310}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p>n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>BUB1</em> and <em>BUB3</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal dominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>{28577310}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p>n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p><em>SETD2</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>Autosomal dominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>{28577310}</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"105\">\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"84\">\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"252\">\r\n<p>Coincidental sporadic MMR mutations; no underlying cause</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>n/a, not applicable.</p>\r\n<p>Notes: Synonyms for LLS include &ldquo;LS mimic&rdquo;, &ldquo;LS-like&rdquo;, and &ldquo;mutation-negative LS&rdquo;. Patients with LLS may represent a heterogeneous group. LLS has a mean age of onset similar to that of LS. At least 50&ndash;60% of LLS-associated colorectal cancers exhibit biallelic somatic inactivation of the MMR genes within the tumour through somatic mutations (nonsense, missense, or frameshift mutations; splice-site deletions; gene deletions; or loss of heterozygosity). LS tumours may themselves have somatic mutations in the same genes in which heritable mutations cause the syndromes that in turn give rise to LLS. The overarching term &ldquo;familial colorectal cancer&nbsp;X (FCC-X)&rdquo; has been used for familial colorectal cancer in which the tumours are microsatellite-stable (i.e. do not have MMR deficiency). Mutations in LLS-associated genes can also be the cause of FCC-X. The potential value of multiple gene test panels and tumour DNA sequencing will be apparent.</p>\r\n<p>Sources: {25110875; 24953332; 27712984; 28195393; 24468183}</p>",
